WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.720
In the lead-up to the release of Justice League,
the central mystery for savvy fans wasn't

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.580
"is Superman going to be in this thing?" but
rather "black suit—yes or no?"

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.900
Prior to November, many would have hedged
toward "yes", considering tie-in merchandise

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.580
hyping up the suit, and an Instagram post
from Henry Cavill that many took to be a close-up

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.660
of the black outfit.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.490
But when the movie hit theaters with a relatively
lean two-hour runtime, the black suit was

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.530
nowhere to be found.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:29.130
As such, viewers expecting the black suit
were left feeling gaslighted, wondering if

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.780
they had imagined the whole thing.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.250
Was this really advertised?

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.480
Maybe that was a Henry Cavill fan account.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.860
Now, thanks to cinematographer Fabian Wagner,
it's finally been confirmed that the suit

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:43.100
did exist, scenes were shot, and they didn't
end up in the final edit.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:48.290
Wagner is fairly clear about this in an interview
with Inverse, responding to a question regarding

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.980
whether or not scenes were shot involving
the black suit:

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:52.520
“There were [scenes shot].

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.190
It’s a cool looking costume.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.960
Sadly, we didn’t see that either in the
final cut.”

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.120
Could the black suit casualty have been the
result of Warner Bros. wanting to distance

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.140
the movie from the aggressively dark tone
of Man of Steel and Batman v Superman?

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:09.039
It would make a lot of sense, considering
what we know now about the movie's troubled

00:01:09.039 --> 00:01:10.039
production.

00:01:10.039 --> 00:01:13.430
Fabian didn't explain what role the black
suit would have played in the film, but the

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:17.259
comics have seen the Man of Steel sport darker
duds on several occasions.

00:01:17.259 --> 00:01:21.219
The most relevant occurrence happened in The
Reign of the Supermen story arc, in which

00:01:21.219 --> 00:01:25.999
Clark returns from the grave with a black
suit and long hair, after the Death of Superman

00:01:25.999 --> 00:01:26.999
arc.

00:01:26.999 --> 00:01:28.110
Where he, you know, dies.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.110
Fighting Doomsday.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.240
Sound familiar?

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.299
Ultimately, Superman's black suit ended up
on the cutting room floor alongside Willem

00:01:34.299 --> 00:01:40.119
Dafoe's appearance as Vulko, most of Robin
Wright's spoken lines, and Cyborg's backstory.

00:01:40.119 --> 00:01:43.179
Just another thing to wish for in that director's
cut.

00:01:43.179 --> 00:01:44.179
Thanks for watching!

